  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15th, 2023. The project has expanded its team multiple times: initially adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture for an onboarding on September 10th, and later welcoming Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). The project has progressed through the design phase, moving into development under lead developer Omar Jensen, and has successfully completed the testing phase, with a celebration planned for October 10th. Financially, the compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000, and a separate training budget of $15,000 was approved for coding teams and project managers. Stakeholder feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. However, a recent communication highlighted critical budget and management roadblocks requiring immediate attention and confirmation."
